<title>GREECE: Greek industrial output down 1.0pct y/y in Aug.</title>
<headline>Greek industrial output down 1.0pct y/y in Aug.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece's industrial production fell provisionally 1.0 percent year-on-year in August after a 0.9 percent rise in July, the National Statistics Service(NSS) said in a statement.</p>
<p>Manufacturing output decreased 2.4 percent year-on-year in August after being unchanged in July, it said.</p>
<p>    INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT	AUG 96*    JUL 96**    AUG 95</p>
<p>    Year-on-year (pct)	-1.0	  0.9	    3.9</p>
<p>    Index (1980=100)	 103.3	113.9	  104.3</p>
<p>    MANUFACTURING OUTPUT   AUG 96*    JUL 96**    AUG 95</p>
<p>    Year-on-year (pct)	-2.4	  0.0	   5.4</p>
<p>    Index (1980=100)	  93.0	103.8	  95.3</p>
<p>*  indicates provisional data</p>
<p>** indicate revised data</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
